From: Jonathan Jackson <70459+jjackson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:19:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Labs mode: scrub credentials from Sentry events

Upstream sends default PII, so Sentry's servlet integration attaches request
headers to events, and even with PII off it only drops its own sensitive-header
list, which does not include X-Labs-HQ-Token. In labs mode a BeforeSend (and
BeforeSendTransaction) callback removes X-Labs-HQ-Token, X-Labs-Signature*,
Authorization, X-MAC-DIGEST and cookies from every event. The PII default is
now configurable (SENTRY_SEND_DEFAULT_PII, default true as upstream).
